# Annotation database schema changes

Deployed annotation databases are created and upgraded only by
`Servers/SQL/DatabaseCreateUpdate/CreateUpdateDatabase.sql`. A change that is not in that script never reaches a real
database.

## What counts

Tables, columns, indexes, constraints, defaults, triggers, views, functions, stored procedures, grants, and changes to a
procedure's body (even `SET NOCOUNT ON` or a one-line fix).

## How to add one

- Append a new step at the end, numbered one past the highest `DBVersionID` in the file. Copy the shape of the steps
  around it:
  - `if(not(exists(select (1) from DBVersion where DBVersionID = N)))`;
  - a `print`;
  - a named `BEGIN TRANSACTION`;
  - each statement in `EXEC('...')`, with quotes doubled;
  - an `@@error` check that rolls back and returns;
  - `INSERT INTO DBVersion values (N, N'<what changed>', getDate(), User_ID())`;
  - `COMMIT TRANSACTION`.
- Never edit an earlier step. Databases that already ran it will not run it again. Fix a past mistake with a new step.
- Change a procedure with `ALTER PROCEDURE` (or drop and recreate) in the new step, starting from its latest definition
  in the script. That is the last step that defines it, not the first one, and not the `.sqlproj` copy.
- A step must be safe on every database the script upgrades: guard object creation with an existence check where an
  earlier hand fix may already have created the object, and never drop or rewrite user data without a decision from
  the user.
- `ALTER DATABASE` cannot run inside a transaction. Follow step 82, which commits `main` first and reopens it.

## The other copies

`Servers/AnnotationDatabase` (the SSDT `.sqlproj`), `Servers/AnnotationDatabase/scripts/minimal-schema.sql` (the smoke
schema for the throwaway test container) and the EF model in `Servers/ConnectomeDataModelCore` are copies for tests and
code. Mirror each `CreateUpdateDatabase.sql` change into whichever of them holds that object, in the same commit, so
tests see what deployed databases will have. A change made only in a copy is not deployed, so never add or change an object in a
copy without the matching `CreateUpdateDatabase.sql` step. (`dbo.DeletedStructures`, added only to `minimal-schema.sql`
and the EF model, is the example of what goes wrong: code came to depend on a table no deployed database has.)

## Before committing

- Run the new step against the throwaway `AnnotationTest` container: first on a database built by the script up to the
  previous version, then a second time to show it is skipped.
- Never run it against a real database. Deploying the script is the user's job.
